<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.860
<b>Film</b>

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.020
Isn't the Transcription Research Group

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.860
famous for discovering the Dead Sea Scrolls?

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.430
No, no!

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.370
It was a portion of the Nag Hammadi library.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.710
Plus, that was forty years ago and 
has nothing to do with any of us.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.710
<b>Shibahama UFO Wars</b>

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.790
More importantly, we need to get the data,
 or there are gonna be problems!

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.170
We're not quite at the date 
stipulated in the contract yet.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.050
But there are parts that are at a standstill!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.840
You realize we're about the only ones

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.430
<b>We should install

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.430
who will go to the trouble of burning 
physical discs anymore, right?

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.380
We've got a lot of work to do,

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.150
and it's not exactly a 
cakewalk to get it all done!

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:49.150
It seems like a bad sign if you're accepting 
more work than you know you can finish.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.540
I wasn't expecting griping 
from such a prestigious club.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.520
Listen, you!

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.020
I hear propellers!

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:00.510
<b>Film</b>

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.160
It's a drone!

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.280
<b>SECURITY CLUB</b>

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.300
It says "security club" on it.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.470
Nice eyesight.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.750
The security club?!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.790
<b>Film</b>

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.790
Something's happening!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.830
<b>Film</b>

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.590
Stop that! I didn't give the order to shoot!

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.060
Freeze!

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.520
Drop your weapons!

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.980
You're under arrest for arranging deals 
using school funds without permission!

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.810
What's all this?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.940
We've already been given permission 
to reproduce media already!

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.190
Not to mention we—

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.610
<b>SECURITY CLUB</b>

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.610
That came from the entrance!

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.990
Don't shoot!

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:48.620
Notice of Expulsion

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.490
The student council's taking it from here.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.130
He's just been expelled with 
prejudice on suspicion

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.620
of illicitly spending school funds 
on an unauthorized exchange.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.570
As of this moment, this entire matter 
is now under our jurisdiction.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.420
You guys, clear on out.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.090
If you don't want to end up 
like this, I'd be careful.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.360
We're not like them.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:07.140
Now, about compensation for 
the broken door and windows...

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.620
<b>• Seven Window Panes

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.890
The school's bound to make a move soon.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.870
The day of Comet A 
will be the day of
 the screening event!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.870
Venue is across from
 Chamber of Commerce!!

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.620
Shibahama Chamber of Commerce
Original Animation
<b>Shibahama UFO Wars</b>
Audition

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.600
<b>Shibahama Water

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.130
It leads here? That's another route scouted!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.570
Why is the vice-principal here on a Sunday?

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:00.810
Neue! Deutsche! Härte!

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.280
Neue! Deutsche! Härte!

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:03.990
Good morning.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.010
Good morning! Guten morgen!

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.580
Guten morgen.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.840
Neue! Deutsche! Härte!

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.950
Cosmos...

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.250
A flower that represents peace...

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.350
What even is an enemy?

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.550
The leaves you can make money off of!

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.940
Values vary, depending on the environment.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.690
What a tasty-looking raccoon dog we've caught.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.020
Is that an ant queen being carried away?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.270
You think you've got the time 
to go out for a stroll?!

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.560
Mercy, please!

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.220
Mercy for the fourth-rate director who 
still doesn't know her own story?!

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.910
A bear!

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:56.190
I'd say the tech marks him 
as a human being, actually.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.750
What's he doing here on a Sunday, though?

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:03.540
I must be present whenever you girls 
are at the school for club activities.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.770
Them's the rules.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:09.260
And with you three, that means
 I basically never get a day off.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.810
Not to mention I'm always here late
 without getting paid overtime...

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.790
Being a club adviser is a lot 
rougher than I imagined.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.450
I figured I'd play video games all day,

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.170
but had trouble deciding on which one.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.020
See, you can't expect 
someone to be able to work

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.790
with no time off or no enjoyment.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.520
Don't work more than you have to,

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.670
and when you find the time to, you play around.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.950
That's the trick to working.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.660
That's it! We haven't 
been playing around enough!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.490
Time to make up for lost time!

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.660
We don't have time for more distractions!

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.010
It'll be a change of pace!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.930
You two have work to do!

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:51.570
Damn it!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.810
The best work comes from a sense of play.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.900
So have fun, young lady.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.820
If you fall off, you'll die!

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.360
I'm already dead, so it's fine.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.250
You still have three more lives!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.650
I've already died six times.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.600
Takamune

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.370
Let's go down here!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.750
There's a river flowing underneath the ground!

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.340
The river to hell!

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:29.340
Underground Tunnel

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.340
There's a sheer cliff on the other side of here!

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.840
This is less making the project fun,
 and more just goofing around

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.930
It's a freaking sheer cliff! We could 
actually die if we fell from here!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.260
Look at you, repeating what I just said like

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:42.430
you're the first one to realize it—

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.630
There's a swing!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:46.450
That thing that looks like it's meant 
for trapping people by the behind?

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:49.020
You'd have to be nuts to get on that thing!

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.740
You could end up biting the big one!

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.950
Aw, man, I wanna swing on it!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.380
I don't think there's a route 
to get down there. How come?

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.970
All roads lead to Rome. 
Maybe you need to go there first.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.750
You'd still need a road <i>from</i> Rome, 
and I don't see any leading to the swing.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.620
Let's take the river, then!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:06.130
Are we headed toward heaven or hell?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.670
Either way, make sure to 
pay the ferryman yourself.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.420
Y'know you cross the river 
Styx widthwise, right?

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.760
That makes the afterlife over there!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.450
So the world we live in is heaven and hell, huh?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.620
No wonder it's so hard to "live" in it!

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.230
What's up, Kanamori?

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.940
Well, I think I just saw a ghost.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.940
<b>Bunny High Altitude ver.</b>

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.940
<b>With Safety Harness to
 Prevent Falls</b>

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.130
Don't!

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.490
Asakusa's sucking on her bunny again.

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.200
It's getting a bit less steep around here.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:45.710
Let's all make this a solar town

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.710
Wow! What is this place?

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.940
It's completely flooded!

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:48.970
There are fish!

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.010
Submarines

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:55.010
Yeah!!!!

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.740
Where's that swing, though?

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.850
On the other side, likely.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.610
I guess we'd have to go through here...

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.970
There's too much water to pass through.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.050
I guess we really do need a sub.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.310
I'm pretty sure this is a road, not a river.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.090
Whuzzat?!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.450
<b>EXIT</b>

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.900
You're right!

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.780
I saw something at the other end of the tunnel!

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.370
Was it a kappa? You think?

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:29.130
Let's all make this a solar town

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.540
We're left with more and more questions...

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:33.090
Let's just say it's a sunken 
city full of kappas.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.720
Nice!

