</b>

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:47.360
<b>Source: A surprising side to Tsubame Mizusaki? Entertainment News</b>

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>"All eyes on Shibahama High School's festival! This robot anime created by students is amazing!"
 "An anime by the famous model Tsubame Mizusaki?!"
 "The next project is a set in the town of Shibahama itself!"</b>

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>Source: Shibahama High School Festival a Huge Success! Shibahama Hot News</b>

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>• Even the internet's talking about it! A look at the anime made by high school students!</b>

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.650
Seems like a big deal...

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>High school model Tsubame Mizusaki 
 produces an anime set in Shibahama!
When will it premiere? And where?</b>

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>• External Link Special Report: "Tsubame Mizusaki's New Venture" Teen's News</b>

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.060
What the heck?!

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:53.680
The press has started promoting us now.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:54.610
Why?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:57.070
"The school is allowing 
students to participate in a"

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:01.370
"local revitalization effort in order 
to teach them about business,"

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:01.370
<b>New Cat Mom @nyan_mam
\h It's so nice for a school to help out locally</b>

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:01.370
<b>Kappanosuke @Cucumbeeeeeee
\h\h\hThink Shiba High is now my first choice for a school</b>

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.870
"a locally-oriented educational 
program that's earning"

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.880
"Shibahama High praise from all around."

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>Well,
 the school's position is...</b>

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>About producing
pamphlets for Shibahama High School—</b>

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>The eizouken's?</b>

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>After watching the
 anime screening?</b>

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>Hello</b>

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>You read an
 article about the eizouken?</b>

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>Really interested in the eizouken's
 activities...</b>

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>Filming for a
local TV program?</b>

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:06.880
<b>Hello</b>

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:11.860
The school has no choice but 
to let us move forward at this point.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.970
Goodness gracious, that sure is something.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.220
So we can finish the short?

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:21.220
Speaking of, is it done? The concept 
for the enemy, and the story?

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.970
You bet your butt!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.190
Es perfecto!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.560
Ta-dah!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.170
An enemy UFO is shot down and crash-lands.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.160
There's a silhouette inside the cockpit....

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.220
The enemy is a kappa!

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:53.190
They didn't come from space, but nearby!

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:55.340
But through a quirk of fate,

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.990
they learn about their history 
as a result of the crash-landing.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.270
As water levels began to rise,

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:12.100
the remaining cities were 
built higher and higher,

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.010
but those forced to live in 
the water eventually found

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.850
their bodies adapting to their new way of life.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.650
The Atlantis Alliance!

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.370
A race from below the waves!

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Gills</b>

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.330
For a while, they communicated

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.040
with their distant brethren with a 
device that worked like a prayer wheel,

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.000
but in time the tradition 
faded and was forgotten,

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.270
leading to ignorance that 
bred fear, and then enmity...

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:36.250
with both sides arming themselves.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.610
That's how land reclamation 
turned into an invasion.

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:43.000
A war waged because of a forgotten kinship...

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.730
Conflict born from focusing 
only on one's own conditions.

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:48.730
A battle rooted in a lack 
of concern for each other.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.470
"The humans we were so afraid of..."

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:07.120
"They're not different 
from us kappas after all!"

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.080
He realizes what they have in common.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:13.330
And at the same time, a human 
enemy has a similar revelation.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.230
Wait, new material?

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:17.820
W-We can manage it by altering 
the footage of the kappa POW,

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.880
so it won't be as much work as it sounds like!

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:23.190
He hears the chime of the 
harmonious prayer bell...

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.140
Things play out the same way.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.470
And the human has the same realization:

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:55.740
"The enemy isn't something dreadful,
 but the same as us."

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.300
The entire conflict spins 
out of the deterioration

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.550
and disrepair of a system for interchange!

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.010
It's war!

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.470
<b>Zoom  Screech  Pow</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.730
Then they both take action.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.330
To repair the signaling device 
that allows for communication

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.910
with the other side, 
and restore trust in each other...

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:13.650
<b>Prayer bell
\h\h\his now buried
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h in dirt</b>

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.480
And to end the war!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.940
<b>Prayer bell
\h\h\his now buried
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h in dirt</b>

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:16.250
<b>This time the light crosses by
 up close in front of the screen</b>

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.250
The POWs don't betray their own kind,

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.860
but become mediators seeking to 
reconcile with their lost kin!

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:30.830
And then...

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.360
<b>Ripples</b>

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.360
<b>Land</b>

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:48.190
Hearing the sound, all parties involved 
learn the truth about each other.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:53.670
They come to an understanding, 
and the fighting stops.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.520
The theme of this work...

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:03.110
is coexistence.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.340
<b>Coexistence</b>

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:12.180
Values are shaped by surroundings.

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:15.750
It's only natural that there'd be 
different ways of looking at things.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:19.210
A mutually beneficial relationship 
of give-and-take...

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.500
And the grand finale is a 
dance party with the kappas!

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:26.800
<b>Dance party with kappas and people begins!</b>

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:26.800
Kappas?

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.660
But I was drawing people in the rough drafts.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.830
They're basically the same shape as humans!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.340
You just need to add a little bowl 
to the top of their heads.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:38.690
Well, I guess that shouldn't be too hard.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.320
11:30?!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:43.650
Are the two of you trying 
to commit sabotage?!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.450
Get back to work, damn it!

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.450
<b>Film</b>

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:56.460
<b>Emergency Containment Tank</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:02.590
<b>A piece with a calm, sensible tone</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.000
<b>Stillness</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.090
<b>For use on c001-012, even-handed and steady sounding,
 with sparse arrangement</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.420
<b>Sign • Premonition</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.460
<b>For use on c025-033, arrangement is gradually starting to become more lively</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.880
<b>Tension</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.920
<b>For use with c050-070, brings to mind tensely played string instruments</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.340
<b>Intensifying</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.380
<b>For use with c090-126, Steadily starts to intensify,
 coming on more strongly, and thrillingly</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Understanding</b>

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>For use on c135-c163. On the sparse side re: arrangement,
 with a gentle, intimate sound</b>

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Battle Pattern 1</b>

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Shibahama comes under attack. Lots of low tones</b>

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Battle Pattern 2</b>

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>UFO vs Steam Tanks. Starting to sound more heated</b>

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Battle Pattern 3</b>

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Fast-paced, the most exciting piece</b>

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Dance Scene</b>

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>Music like you'd hear at an elegant ball</b>

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:04.630
<b>A bright, fun-sounding piece</b>

